Routes added (must match registry exactly so 9999 final gate
passes):
  Backend:   POST /api/v1/ai/power/sql/draft
  Frontend:  /power/sql
  UITestIDs: [ai-feature-nl-sql-playground-root]
  JobNames:  []
  PushKinds: []

Tools (typed propose-only):
  - draft_readonly_sql:    {prompt,sql,rationale} ⇒ ReadonlySQLDraft DTO
  - validate_readonly_sql: ReadonlySQLDraft ⇒ {ok,reason}
  Both refuse any keyword in the deny-list (INSERT, UPDATE,
  DELETE, DROP, ALTER, CREATE, TRUNCATE, GRANT, REVOKE, VACUUM,
  COPY, CALL, DO, MERGE, EXECUTE) and any table reference outside
  the per-request scope-bound curated catalog.

Curated install-wide schema catalog (hardcoded, 5 tables):
  drives, charging_sessions, vehicles, alerts, signal_log_view —
  with SI canonical fields (distance_m, energy_used_wh,
  avg_speed_mps, etc.) per Phase-48 SI cutover.

=== REASONING ===
ADR-015 alignment (every invariant this slice touches):
  I1 default-off:    nl-sql-playground registry entry has
                     DefaultOn: false. Verified by registry
                     coverage test in features/registry_test.go.
  I3 baseline intact: SqlPlaygroundPage renders the manual SQL
                     editor + curated catalog REGARDLESS of the
                     AI feature toggle's state. The AI drafter
                     section is rendered alongside via
                     withAiFeature so it is the only thing that
                     toggles; the baseline never goes away.
  I4 zero egress:    With ai_mode='off' the route returns 404 via
                     ai.GuardedHandler (proven by Go-side
                     TestNLSQLPlaygroundAIOffManualSQLWorks). No
                     provider call path is reachable.
  I5 hidden UI:      AINLSqlPlayground is wrapped by
                     withAiFeature('nl-sql-playground', ...) so
                     the entire AI section is ABSENT from the DOM
                     in off mode (proven by SPA off-mode test).
  I6 404 routes:     guard wrapper ai.GuardedHandler returns 404
                     when settings.ai_mode='off' OR the per-feature
                     toggle is false (Go-side test pins both with
                     the stubGuardSettings table).
  I7 per-feature:    ai_features['nl-sql-playground'] toggle is
                     respected ON TOP of mode='off'. The Go-side
                     tests pin BOTH (mode=off+toggle=on and
                     mode=cloud+toggle=false return 404).
  I8 propose-only:   tools.draft_readonly_sql and
                     tools.validate_readonly_sql ONLY construct
                     and validate a typed DTO; they do not execute
                     SQL or touch the database. The SPA's "Apply
                     to editor" button copies the typed draft into
                     the manual SQL editor's state via the onApply
                     prop — the LLM never writes editor state
                     directly. The user must then explicitly click
                     the canonical Run button.
  I10 type system:   ReadonlySQLDraft DTO is shared between Go
                     (internal/ai/tools/nl_sql_playground.go) and
                     TypeScript (web/src/components/ai/
                     AINLSqlPlayground.tsx) with field-name parity
                     (json:"prompt", json:"sql", json:"rationale",
                     json:"referenced_tables").
  I12 client/bg:     Service-worker chunk name 'ai-nl-sql-playground'
                     is encoded by the lazy-import naming
                     (web/src/App.tsx imports
                     ./features/power-user/pages/SqlPlaygroundPage
                     which lazy-imports AINLSqlPlayground via
                     withAiFeature). LocalStorage key
                     'ai.sqlPlayground.draft' is the only client
                     storage artifact this slice adds; it is
                     populated by the deterministic baseline
                     editor and is NOT AI-only (it persists the
                     manual SQL editor's contents irrespective of
                     AI mode), so it survives mode toggles
                     without leaking AI artifacts.

P1 (provider port):       provider calls flow through the F1
                          provider port; no direct adapter import.
P5 (decorator chain):     all provider calls flow through the
                          locked decorator chain (redaction →
                          rate limit → cost cap → audit → trace)
                          via the shared dispatch.
P6 (backend guard +       backend route wrapped with
   frontend feature       ai.GuardedHandler; SPA component wrapped
   gating):               with withAiFeature.
P7 (predecessor):         all foundation predecessors verified
                          STATUS=DONE in PREFLIGHT.
P8 (eval goldens):        4 deterministic goldens (>= 3 required)
                          + 4 canned mock-provider replies.
P9 (registry coverage):   nl-sql-playground entry has all
                          RouteSet fields populated explicitly
                          (empty arrays for jobs/push, not omitted).
P10 (baseline coexistence): SqlPlaygroundPage renders manual
                            editor + curated catalog regardless of
                            toggle state.
P11 (wired or absent):    AINLSqlPlayground imports useAiStream
                          and POSTs against the registered
                          backend endpoint; on-mode wiring test
                          proves SSE round-trip.
P12 (no placeholder       no "future slice" / "coming soon" /
    buttons):             "wiring lands" / "would call POST"
                          strings (W1 placeholder scan = 0).

Selection mechanism (P10 baseline coexistence):
  The SqlPlaygroundPage ALWAYS renders the manual SQL editor +
  curated catalog. The optional AI drafter section
  (AINLSqlPlayground) is rendered alongside via withAiFeature, so
  it is entirely absent in off-mode (ADR-015 §I5+§I6) and propose-
  only in on-mode (ADR-015 §I8 — the user must explicitly click
  the canonical Apply to editor button to copy the LLM's proposal
  into the textarea, then must explicitly click the canonical
  Run button to execute).

